Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(secure-connect): system kill switch (Windows
 Firewall) for TUN mode
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a WireSock-style network lock that puts Windows Firewall into
default-deny outbound while a TUN profile is connected, so no traffic can
leak outside the tunnel — even if the core drops or during connect/disconnect.

- ServiceLib/Manager/KillSwitch/: platform backend (interface, manager,
  Windows impl via NetSecurity, no-op stub, context + persisted state)
- Config: KillSwitchItem (enable, allow LAN, split-tunnel bypass lists)
- CoreManager: arm after a successful TUN connect (idempotent on reload,
  fail-closed on mid-session core restart)
- AppManager: disarm on app exit; MainWindowViewModel: recover on startup
  (unlock if a previous run crashed while armed)

First step of the v2rayN -> Secure Connect fork; see FORK-ROADMAP.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
